# state: first-run   (recorded creating the profile; lane.savestate433)
# Burnout 3: Takedown (4541005B), FIRST RUN: a disk with no Burnout 3
# profile. DRAFT, not yet played: written from pass 1's frames
# (0-0-y-1790433159-titleplay-p1-burnout3, Thor, 2026-09-26), which show:
#
#   ~20 s RenderWare, ~40 s attract FMV, ~60 s "Press START to continue";
#   START -> Select Language (English highlighted);
#   A -> "Burnout 3 requires a Profile ... LOAD PROFILE / NEW PROFILE",
#        NEW PROFILE highlighted;
#   A -> DRIVER DETAILS keyboard, name BURNOUT, `Done` highlighted;
#   A -> "Would you like to save your profile? YES / NO", NO highlighted.
#
# Pass 1 answered A there, which is NO, then "Autosave will be disabled. Are
# you sure?" and A again: a loop it never left. The answer is UP, then A.
# What follows YES (a storage prompt, a "saving" notice) was never seen, so
# from `mark profile-saved` on this route goes back to surveying: frames at
# every step, and no `mark gameplay`. The navigating agent's pilot replaces
# that part with what it actually finds.
#
# UP is the left stick pushed and released, not the D-pad: pad.sh maps UP to
# BTN_DPAD_UP (544), and whether the Thor's pad reports its D-pad as keys or
# as a hat has not been checked. A stick flick works in both cases.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
mark booted
press START
wait 4
shot language
press A
wait 4
shot select-option
press A
wait 4
shot keyboard
press A
wait 4
shot save-prompt
axis LY min
wait 0.3
axis LY mid
wait 1
shot save-prompt-yes
press A
wait 8
shot after-yes
mark profile-saved
repeat 8 {
    press A
    wait 5
    shot after-save
}
mark play
repeat forever {
    repeat 2 {
        axis RT max
        press A
        wait 10
        axis RT mid
        wait 1
    }
    shot play
}
